            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did kākkai mean, and what did paṟavai mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: தயிர்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தயிர் (tayir) — \"curd\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set பால், soured overnight in a covered pot. It is what a Tamil meal finishes on, turned through the last of the சாதம், and it is the thing a hot afternoon is survived with."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The sisters do not agree here at all: Kannada ಮೊಸರು (mosaru), Telugu పెరుగు (perugu), Tamil தயிர் (tayir). Three households, three words, one pot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five kitchen words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
