        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: நெய்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நெய் (ney) — \"ghee\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Butter cooked down until the water has gone and only the fat and the smell are left. Short, old, and Tamil's own. Telugu keeps it as నెయ్యి (neyyi); Kannada walked off to ತುಪ್ಪ (tuppa)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A spoon of it goes over hot சாதம் at the start of a meal on a day that matters, which is most of what it does."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ney",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ney*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "tayir, then ney, and say which one ends a meal and which one opens it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *tayir*, then *ney*, and say which one ends a meal and which one opens it]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
