        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: எண்ணெய்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எண்ணெய் (eṇṇey) — \"oil\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The end of it is நெய் (ney), standing there unchanged. The front piece is an old name for the sesame seed, so the whole thing began as sesame-fat — and then it widened until it covered every oil a kitchen has, sesame or not."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kannada kept the same word as ಎಣ್ಣೆ (eṇṇe); Telugu went to నూనె (nūne). The doubled ண் in the middle is the one made with the tongue curled back, held twice as long."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and the third is built out of the second."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
