          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சர்க்கரை (sarkkarai) — \"sugar\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The refined white kind, beside வெல்லம் (vellam) rather than in place of it. Kannada ಸಕ್ಕರೆ (sakkare), Telugu చక్కెర (cakkera): one word, lightly redressed three times."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It has travelled further than any other word in this run. Sanskrit śarkarā went out through Arabic, Greek and Latin and came back into English as sugar, so சர்க்கரை (sarkkarai) and the English word are one word wearing different clothes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: curd, ghee, oil, jaggery, and sugar."
            }
          ]
        },
